# Without this, GitHub-hosted Windows runners' default git config
# (core.autocrlf=true) silently converts these to CRLF on checkout —
# harmless for most text files, but fatal for unified diffs: `git apply`
# parses them byte-exactly, and a stray \r on a blank context line breaks
# hunk parsing ("error: corrupt patch at line N"). Confirmed: this broke
# vendor-patches/espeak-rs-sys-windows-cross-compile.patch specifically in
# .github/workflows/release.yml's Windows job (git apply), even though the
# same file applies fine via `patch -p1` on the Linux jobs, which don't do
# this conversion by default.
*.patch text eol=lf
justfile text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
